# The same rules, for the case where EAS archives from this directory rather
# than from the repository root.
#
# Which one it picks depends on how it resolves the project root, and the
# answer has changed between CLI versions. Both files are correct on their own
# terms, and having both means a build cannot be large — or leak an env file —
# because the archive root was not the one expected.
#
# See ../.easignore for why this denies rather than permits.

node_modules/
.expo/
android/
ios/
*.log

# Build-time values come from the `env` block of the chosen profile in
# eas.json, never from a file here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
